IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cla-nouns`
IMPORT `cla-seat`

-- Civil Law Act 1909 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 15/10/2024)
-- LAYER 2 -- WORKED CASES for the seat questions in cla-seat.l4: at least one case per question, with the facts a real person in the seat
-- would state, and the answer the Act gives; a case marked "NOTHING" is a case the Act does not answer.

§ `Cases for the seat questions`

§§ `Courts and equity (ss 3 and 4)`

#ASSERT `Must the court give me the equitable relief I claim` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- an equitable claim in a civil case
#ASSERT `Must the court give me the equitable relief I claim` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- a claim that is not equitable
#ASSERT `Must the court give me the equitable relief I claim` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a civil case in the court

#ASSERT `May the tenant commit voluntary waste` `Tenant for life or lives` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a tenant for life, no special right
#ASSERT `May the tenant commit voluntary waste` `Leasehold tenant` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a leasehold tenant, no special right
#ASSERT `May the tenant commit voluntary waste` `Leasehold tenant` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- an estate without impeachment of waste
#ASSERT `May the tenant commit voluntary waste` `Another kind of occupier` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- another kind of occupier

#ASSERT `Is the tenant liable to me in damages for voluntary waste` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- waste in breach of s 4(3)
#ASSERT `Is the tenant liable to me in damages for voluntary waste` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- no breach of s 4(3)

#ASSERT `May I sue for possession in my own name only` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- entitled, no notice, no joint contract
#ASSERT `May I sue for possession in my own name only` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the mortgagee has given notice
#ASSERT `May I sue for possession in my own name only` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a joint contract
#ASSERT `May I sue for possession in my own name only` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not entitled to possession

#ASSERT `Is my assignment of the debt effectual in law` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- absolute, written, notice given
#ASSERT `Is my assignment of the debt effectual in law` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- no notice yet
#ASSERT `Is my assignment of the debt effectual in law` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- by way of charge only

#ASSERT `From what date does the legal right pass to me` TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 14 3 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST (Date 14 3 2025) -- notice given on 14 March 2025
#ASSERT `From what date does the legal right pass to me` TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 14 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- no notice given

#ASSERT `Has the legal right passed to me by a day` TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 14 3 2025) TRUE (Date 13 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the day before the notice
#ASSERT `Has the legal right passed to me by a day` TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 14 3 2025) TRUE (Date 14 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the day of the notice
#ASSERT `Has the legal right passed to me by a day` TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 14 3 2025) FALSE (Date 15 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING -- no notice given

#ASSERT `Can I give a good discharge for the debt` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- absolute, written, notice given
#ASSERT `Can I give a good discharge for the debt` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- no notice yet
#ASSERT `Can I give a good discharge for the debt` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- by way of charge only

#ASSERT `Is time of the essence of my contract` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- equity would not have treated it as of the essence
#ASSERT `Is time of the essence of my contract` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- equity would have treated it as of the essence

#ASSERT `May the court grant me an interlocutory injunction` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- just or convenient
#ASSERT `May the court grant me an interlocutory injunction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not shown to be just or convenient

#ASSERT `May the court grant interim relief for my foreign proceedings` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a civil matter abroad, just and convenient
#ASSERT `May the court grant interim relief for my foreign proceedings` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not just or convenient
#ASSERT `May the court grant interim relief for my foreign proceedings` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- a fiscal matter
#ASSERT `May the court grant interim relief for my foreign proceedings` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- proceedings in Singapore only

§§ `Gaming, wagering, maintenance and funding of claims (ss 5, 5A and 5B)`

#ASSERT `Is my gaming or wagering contract null and void` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a plain wager
#ASSERT `Is my gaming or wagering contract null and void` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a subscription for a prize
#ASSERT `Is my gaming or wagering contract null and void` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a totalisator bet
#ASSERT `Is my gaming or wagering contract null and void` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not gaming or wagering

#ASSERT `May I sue to recover a sum won on a wager` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a plain wager
#ASSERT `May I sue to recover a sum won on a wager` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- a licensed operator's contract
#ASSERT `May I sue to recover a sum won on a wager` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a wager

#ASSERT `Is my totalisator bet within the exceptions` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a totalisator bet
#ASSERT `Is my totalisator bet within the exceptions` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- another bet

#ASSERT `Is my promise to repay a sum paid under a void wager null` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a promise to repay
#ASSERT `Is my promise to repay a sum paid under a void wager null` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a promise of commission
#ASSERT `Is my promise to repay a sum paid under a void wager null` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- another promise

#ASSERT `Am I liable in tort for maintenance or champerty` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- liability only for maintenance or champerty
#ASSERT `Am I liable in tort for maintenance or champerty` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- liability on another footing

#ASSERT `Is my third-party funding contract illegal as maintenance or champerty` TRUE Yes EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a funder funds prescribed proceedings
#ASSERT `Is my third-party funding contract illegal as maintenance or champerty` TRUE No EQUALS NOTHING -- not prescribed proceedings
#ASSERT `Is my third-party funding contract illegal as maintenance or champerty` TRUE `I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING -- not sure the proceedings are prescribed
#ASSERT `Is my third-party funding contract illegal as maintenance or champerty` FALSE Yes EQUALS NOTHING -- no funder

#ASSERT `Must I comply with the prescribed requirements for third-party funding` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a funder or funded party
#ASSERT `Must I comply with the prescribed requirements for third-party funding` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- anyone else

#ASSERT `Have I complied with the prescribed requirements for third-party funding` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- complied
#ASSERT `Have I complied with the prescribed requirements for third-party funding` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not complied
#ASSERT `Have I complied with the prescribed requirements for third-party funding` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- the duty does not arise

#ASSERT `May the funder enforce its rights under the funding contract` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- ceased to qualify, no relief
#ASSERT `May the funder enforce its rights under the funding contract` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- relief granted
#ASSERT `May the funder enforce its rights under the funding contract` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- a right not connected with it

§§ `Contracts that must be in writing, trusts, the euro (ss 6 to 9)`

#ASSERT `May I bring an action on this promise without a signed writing` `Action on a special promise to answer for the debt default or miscarriage of another person` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a guarantee, nothing in writing
#ASSERT `May I bring an action on this promise without a signed writing` `Action on a special promise to answer for the debt default or miscarriage of another person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- a guarantee, signed writing
#ASSERT `May I bring an action on this promise without a signed writing` `Another kind of action` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- another kind of action

#ASSERT `Is my action barred for want of a signed writing` `Action on a contract for the sale or other disposition of immovable property or an interest in it` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a contract for the sale of land, nothing in writing
#ASSERT `Is my action barred for want of a signed writing` `Action on a contract for the sale or other disposition of immovable property or an interest in it` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the same, signed writing
#ASSERT `Is my action barred for want of a signed writing` `Another kind of action` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- another kind of action

#ASSERT `Is my declaration of trust of immovable property properly proved` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a signed writing
#ASSERT `Is my declaration of trust of immovable property properly proved` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- made by will
#ASSERT `Is my declaration of trust of immovable property properly proved` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- oral only
#ASSERT `Is my declaration of trust of immovable property properly proved` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not about immovable property

#ASSERT `Is the rule in Bain v Fothergill abolished for my contract` (Date 1 1 1999) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- made on 1 January 1999
#ASSERT `Is the rule in Bain v Fothergill abolished for my contract` (Date 31 12 1998) EQUALS NOTHING -- made the day before

#ASSERT `In what currency may performance be made after the euro` TRUE `The euro` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the euro
#ASSERT `In what currency may performance be made after the euro` TRUE `The currency originally designated in the instrument and still legal tender` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the original currency, still legal tender
#ASSERT `In what currency may performance be made after the euro` TRUE `Any other currency` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- any other currency
#ASSERT `In what currency may performance be made after the euro` FALSE `The euro` EQUALS NOTHING -- performance not possible in the original currency

§§ `Death, expectation of life, interest, charges, the husband (ss 10 to 14)`

#ASSERT `Does my cause of action survive the death` TRUE `Another cause of action` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a debt claim
#ASSERT `Does my cause of action survive the death` TRUE Defamation EQUALS JUST FALSE -- defamation
#ASSERT `Does my cause of action survive the death` FALSE `Another cause of action` EQUALS NOTHING -- nothing subsisted at death

#ASSERT `May the estate recover this head of damages` TRUE `Exemplary damages` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- exemplary damages
#ASSERT `May the estate recover this head of damages` TRUE `Another head of damages` EQUALS NOTHING -- another head

#ASSERT `Can I recover damages for loss of expectation of life` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- personal injuries, not loss of income
#ASSERT `Can I recover damages for loss of expectation of life` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- loss of income
#ASSERT `Can I recover damages for loss of expectation of life` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a personal injuries action

#ASSERT `May the court award me interest on my debt or damages` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the court thinks fit
#ASSERT `May the court award me interest on my debt or damages` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the court does not think fit
#ASSERT `May the court award me interest on my debt or damages` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not such proceedings

#ASSERT `Can I charge my interest in a debt owed to me` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a charge over a debt owed to me, in favour of the debtor
#ASSERT `Can I charge my interest in a debt owed to me` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- in favour of a third person

#ASSERT `Is a husband liable for his wife's torts and earlier debts` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- only because he is her husband
#ASSERT `Is a husband liable for his wife's torts and earlier debts` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- a liability on another footing

§§ `Contribution between persons liable for the same damage (ss 15 to 19)`

#ASSERT `May I recover contribution from the other person liable for the same damage` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- both liable for the same damage
#ASSERT `May I recover contribution from the other person liable for the same damage` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the other is not liable for it

#ASSERT `May I recover contribution after settling the claim` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- settled and would have been liable
#ASSERT `May I recover contribution after settling the claim` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- settled but would not have been liable
#ASSERT `May I recover contribution after settling the claim` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- no settlement

#ASSERT `How much at most can I be required to pay by way of contribution` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 8000 5000 EQUALS JUST 5000 -- a contribution above the limited damages
#ASSERT `How much at most can I be required to pay by way of contribution` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 3000 5000 EQUALS JUST 3000 -- a contribution within the limit
#ASSERT `How much at most can I be required to pay by way of contribution` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 8000 5000 EQUALS NOTHING -- no limit or reduction

#ASSERT `Am I entitled to costs when several actions were brought` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a later action, no reasonable ground
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to costs when several actions were brought` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- a later action, reasonable ground
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to costs when several actions were brought` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the first judgment
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to costs when several actions were brought` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- only one action

#ASSERT `Do the contribution sections apply to damage before 1 January 1999` (Date 31 12 1998) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 31 December 1998
#ASSERT `Do the contribution sections apply to damage before 1 January 1999` (Date 1 1 1999) EQUALS NOTHING -- 1 January 1999

§§ `Death caused by a wrongful act (ss 20 to 22)`

#ASSERT `Is the wrongdoer liable to an action for a death` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- all met
#ASSERT `Is the wrongdoer liable to an action for a death` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no wrongful act
#ASSERT `Is the wrongdoer liable to an action for a death` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not the person who would have been liable

#ASSERT `Am I a dependant of the deceased` `A child grandchild or great-grandchild of the deceased` `By blood` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a child by blood
#ASSERT `Am I a dependant of the deceased` `A child grandchild or great-grandchild of the deceased` `As a stepchild` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a stepchild
#ASSERT `Am I a dependant of the deceased` `A child grandchild or great-grandchild of the deceased` `By adoption into the family of someone else` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a child adopted into another family
#ASSERT `Am I a dependant of the deceased` `Another relationship` `By blood` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- another relationship

#ASSERT `Is my wrongful-death action brought in time` (Date 15 7 2025) (Date 16 7 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the day after the death
#ASSERT `Is my wrongful-death action brought in time` (Date 15 7 2025) (Date 15 7 2028) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the last day
#ASSERT `Is my wrongful-death action brought in time` (Date 15 7 2025) (Date 16 7 2028) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the day after the last day

#ASSERT `May I claim damages for bereavement` `Surviving wife or husband of the deceased` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the surviving spouse
#ASSERT `May I claim damages for bereavement` `Surviving child of the deceased` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a child, with a surviving spouse
#ASSERT `May I claim damages for bereavement` `Surviving brother or sister of the deceased` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a brother with nobody else
#ASSERT `May I claim damages for bereavement` `Not in any of these classes` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not in any class

#ASSERT `What sum is awarded as damages for bereavement` TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST 15000 -- no substituted sum
#ASSERT `What sum is awarded as damages for bereavement` TRUE 20000 EQUALS JUST 20000 -- a substituted sum
#ASSERT `What sum is awarded as damages for bereavement` FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING -- not damages under section 21

#ASSERT `Is this item taken into account in assessing the dependants' damages` TRUE `A sum paid or payable under a contract of assurance or insurance` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- an insurance payment
#ASSERT `Is this item taken into account in assessing the dependants' damages` TRUE `A pension or gratuity paid or payable as a result of the death` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a pension
#ASSERT `Is this item taken into account in assessing the dependants' damages` TRUE `Another item` EQUALS NOTHING -- another item

§§ `Estates, rents and the survivorship of the dead (ss 24 to 30)`

#ASSERT `Is the executor a trustee of the residue for the person entitled on intestacy` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- undisposed residue, no contrary intention
#ASSERT `Is the executor a trustee of the residue for the person entitled on intestacy` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the executor was meant to take it
#ASSERT `Is the executor a trustee of the residue for the person entitled on intestacy` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not undisposed residue

#ASSERT `Can the devisee make the estate pay off the mortgage` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no contrary intention
#ASSERT `Can the devisee make the estate pay off the mortgage` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- a contrary intention
#ASSERT `Can the devisee make the estate pay off the mortgage` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not the devisee

#ASSERT `Is my tenant who held over chargeable with double rent` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- holding over, landlord opts
#ASSERT `Is my tenant who held over chargeable with double rent` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- holding over, no option
#ASSERT `Is my tenant who held over chargeable with double rent` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not holding over

#ASSERT `Must I as a subtenant give notice of the landlord's claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- served, a subtenant who occupies
#ASSERT `Must I as a subtenant give notice of the landlord's claim` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not an occupier

#ASSERT `Have I given my immediate landlord notice forthwith` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- notice given forthwith
#ASSERT `Have I given my immediate landlord notice forthwith` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- no notice
#ASSERT `Have I given my immediate landlord notice forthwith` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- the duty does not arise

#ASSERT `Is the death of two people presumed to have been in order of seniority` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- uncertain, title to property, no order
#ASSERT `Is the death of two people presumed to have been in order of seniority` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a court order
#ASSERT `Is the death of two people presumed to have been in order of seniority` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not for title to property

§§ `Settlements: accumulation, perpetuities, powers (ss 31 to 34)`

#ASSERT `For how long may income be accumulated under an older settlement` (Date 14 12 2004) `A term of 21 years from the date of the making of the disposition` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 21 years from the making
#ASSERT `For how long may income be accumulated under an older settlement` (Date 14 12 2004) `None of these periods` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- none of the periods
#ASSERT `For how long may income be accumulated under an older settlement` (Date 14 12 2004) `None of these periods` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- a provision for debts
#ASSERT `For how long may income be accumulated under an older settlement` (Date 15 12 2004) `The life of the grantor or settlor` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- a settlement made on or after 15 December 2004

#ASSERT `When does the 21-year term from the death end` (Date 15 7 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 7 2021) -- an ordinary day
#ASSERT `When does the 21-year term from the death end` (Date 29 2 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2021) -- a term that would end on a Sunday

#ASSERT `What is the perpetuity period` TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 100 -- none specified
#ASSERT `What is the perpetuity period` TRUE FALSE 80 EQUALS JUST 80 -- 80 years specified
#ASSERT `What is the perpetuity period` TRUE FALSE 150 EQUALS JUST 100 -- 150 years specified
#ASSERT `What is the perpetuity period` TRUE TRUE 80 EQUALS JUST 100 -- lives in being
#ASSERT `What is the perpetuity period` FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING -- the rule does not apply

#ASSERT `Can my disposition yet be treated as invalid for remoteness` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- not yet certain
#ASSERT `Can my disposition yet be treated as invalid for remoteness` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- now certain
#ASSERT `Can my disposition yet be treated as invalid for remoteness` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- would not be invalid anyway

§§ `Minors who have attained 18, and medical advice (ss 35 to 37)`

#ASSERT `Does my contract have effect as if I were of full age` (Date 15 3 2007) (Date 15 3 2025) FALSE `Another kind of contract` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- an ordinary contract on the 18th birthday
#ASSERT `Does my contract have effect as if I were of full age` (Date 15 3 2007) (Date 15 3 2025) FALSE `Contract for a lease of land for more than 3 years` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a lease of more than 3 years
#ASSERT `Does my contract have effect as if I were of full age` (Date 15 3 2007) (Date 15 3 2025) FALSE `Contract for a lease of land not exceeding 3 years` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a lease of land not exceeding 3 years
#ASSERT `Does my contract have effect as if I were of full age` (Date 15 3 2007) (Date 14 3 2025) FALSE `Another kind of contract` EQUALS NOTHING -- a contract the day before the 18th birthday

#ASSERT `May I conduct this legal proceeding in my own name` TRUE TRUE Yes EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a Schedule proceeding
#ASSERT `May I conduct this legal proceeding in my own name` TRUE TRUE No EQUALS NOTHING -- not in the Schedule
#ASSERT `May I conduct this legal proceeding in my own name` TRUE TRUE `I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING -- not sure it is in the Schedule
#ASSERT `May I conduct this legal proceeding in my own name` TRUE FALSE Yes EQUALS NOTHING -- under another legal disability

#ASSERT `Did the healthcare professional meet the standard of care for medical advice` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- every limb met
#ASSERT `Did the healthcare professional meet the standard of care for medical advice` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the opinion supports non-provision on weaker grounds
#ASSERT `Did the healthcare professional meet the standard of care for medical advice` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the opinion is not internally consistent

